<!--
  Silence, which this module has been claiming to have since it was written.

  The pom asks for slf4j-nop "so a no-op binding keeps the runner silent instead of warning on
  every scenario". Logback arrives transitively behind one of the participants and WINS the
  provider race — SLF4J says so on every run ("Actual provider is of type LogbackServiceProvider")
  — so every scenario has been printing the participants' INFO lines all along.

  It cost nothing while a run was sixty-six scenarios. It stops being free the moment the races
  next door run the same participants tens of thousands of times: the log, not the search, was
  the slow part, and it filled the disk before it filled the report.

  Nothing in this module asserts on a log line. The three services that DO assert on theirs do it
  in their own repositories, against their own configuration.
-->
<configuration>
    <root level="OFF"/>
</configuration>
